# Windows launcher scripts must be checked out with CRLF endings.
#
# cmd.exe splits LF-only batch files at the wrong boundaries, so a LF checkout turns the
# launchers into a wall of "'xxx' is not recognized as an internal or external command"
# and nothing opens. Declaring it here fixes every clone, download and ZIP at once,
# instead of depending on each user's core.autocrlf.
# Treat every file as text and let Git normalise it. Without this rule the working tree keeps
# whatever the cloner's core.autocrlf happens to be, so the same revision arrives with different
# bytes on different machines.
* text=auto

# The reader is the artefact users run, it was generated with CRLF, and three of its lines used to
# be bare LF — which made every incidental edit show a three-line unrelated diff. Pin it explicitly.
*.html text eol=crlf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
